``peat pillage`` and the ``pillage`` configuration section are deprecated, and will be removed in a future release. ``peat pillage -P SOURCE`` now runs ``peat parse --copy-files SOURCE``, so it also parses the files it finds, and copies them to ``peat_results/<run-dir>/parse_files/`` instead of ``./pillage_results/``. The ``filenames`` and ``extensions`` in a ``pillage`` section are added to ``collect_file_patterns``, and ``auto_copy``, ``recursive``, and ``locations`` are ignored. The ``peat.api.pillage_api`` module is now ``peat.api.disk_image_api``.
